        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
        ":question/problem": "What is the value of $\\frac{2}{3}\\int_{1}^{e}\\frac{3\\operatorname{ln}(4\\left(\\frac{x}{1}\\right))}{2\\left(\\frac{x}{1}\\right)}\\,\\text{d}x?$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Let's set $u=\\ln\\left(4 \\left(\\frac{x}{1}\\right)\\right).$ Then  we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}\\,\u27f9\\,1\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives the following:\n\n| $x$ | $1$ | $e$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $\\operatorname{ln}\u20614$ | $\\operatorname{ln}\u20614e$ |\n\nWe now substitute and evaluate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3}\\int_{1}^{e}\\frac{3\\operatorname{ln}(4\\left(\\frac{x}{1}\\right))}{2\\left(\\frac{x}{1}\\right)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ & =1\\int_{1}^{e}\\operatorname{ln}(4\\left(\\frac{x}{1}\\right))\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\left(\\frac{x}{1}\\right)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ & =1\\int_{\\operatorname{ln}4}^{\\operatorname{ln}4e}u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\ & =\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot\\left(\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot {\\frac{{u}^{2}}{2}}\\right)|_{\\operatorname{ln}4}^{\\operatorname{ln}4e} \\\\ & =\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot\\left({\\frac{3}{4}\\cdot {u}^{2}}\\right)|_{\\operatorname{ln}4}^{\\operatorname{ln}4e} \\\\ & =\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot\\left(\\frac{3}{4}((\\operatorname{ln}4e)^{2}-(\\operatorname{ln}4)^{2})\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$",
